# Jira authentication is managed by Passman, not this file.
#
# Open Passman, unlock your vault, and enable "Accessible for agents". Then
# create one entry per configured Jira host, named jira-<host>, with a protected
# custom field named `token`:
#
#   Entry: jira-acme
#   Field: token (protected)
#
# This legacy example is kept so older checkouts do not fail when referenced;
# do not put real credentials in .tokens.yaml. The Jira CLI reads Passman via
# its local desktop-agent socket.
